  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-12 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Family Life and Human Development - Early Childhood Development Emphasis program page (poid=10824) and its linked official degree map, 'Family Life & Human Development Degree Maps (2026-2027)', tab 'Early Childhood (Campus)', last updated/reviewed August 3, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. Collected as the BS: the catalog prints a single combined Total Credits, BA/BS Degree: 120, and the map expressly states that students electing the BA take 16 credits of one foreign language, which are not included in the map. All courses must be passed with a C (2.0) or better to be counted in the major (catalog program information). Every semester's courses sum to the map's printed semester total (15/16/15/15/15/15/15/14) and the plan to the catalog's printed Total Credits, BA/BS Degree: 120. The catalog curriculum reconciles exactly: FLHD Core Requirements 30 (ten 3-credit courses, all placed on the map) plus Early Childhood Development Required Courses 32 (itemized 3+3+3+3+0+3+0+3+3+4+3+1+3, including the 0-credit Guidance Lab FLHD 2611 and Play and Creative Experiences Lab FLHD 2621, recorded as required_zero, and the 4-credit FLHD 4880 practicum and 1-credit PE 1543) = the printed Curriculum of 62. The department recommends MATH 1040 - Statistical Inference for the GE Quantitative Literacy requirement; the map prints that first-term row only as 'MATH GE Quantitative Literacy*', recorded as a generic GE choice slot as printed. The catalog's Recommended Elective FLHD 4400 is not placed on the map and is not placed here. The map's free rows total 36 credits (18 Free Electives + 18 Free Upper-division Electives), recorded as printed; the catalog prints no free-elective figure. PE 1543 may be satisfied by a current completion card at graduation (map footnote). GE and elective rows printed without course codes are recorded as choice slots with synthetic codes.",
